## Iron Rules

1. **Docs first**: for any product feature or major technical decision change, edit `docs/design/tech-design.md` first, then the code. Both may land in the same batch, but within a batch the doc must precede the code—never backfill afterwards. The format of `docs/design/tech-design.md` must not deviate from `docs/template/tech-design-template.md`.
2. **Single task list `TODOS.md`**: before starting work, write the task into `TODOS.md` and set it `in_progress` (only one globally at a time); mark `done` only after **code is complete and tests pass**. Never announce completion only in conversation without updating the file.
3. **Language**: technical documentation ({{docs language, default Chinese}}) is written in the docs language; commit messages, identifiers, API names, and **all error messages and logs in code** (error/log/console, event/condition messages, API error responses, CLI runtime output) are written in English. Comments explain "why" in the docs language.
4. **Comments** explain "why" only, never restate the code; no long chains of reasoning.

## Git and Auto-Commit

- Commit messages: English, conventional commits (`feat|fix|docs|refactor|test|chore|perf|ci|build`), imperative mood, subject ≤72 chars, one commit does one thing.
- Before committing manually, run: `git status && git diff && git log --oneline -5`.
- `.opencode/plugins/auto-commit.js` runs `git add -A` (including untracked files, respecting `.gitignore`) on **every session idle** and commits automatically with an LLM-generated message; it commits but never pushes. Therefore:
  - Check `git status` before manual commits—the hook may already have committed, avoid empty/duplicate commits.
  - `.gitignore` is the only defense line: secrets, `.env`, `node_modules`, and build artifacts must be confirmed ignored, or the hook will stage them into commits; when adding a new toolchain, add ignore rules before installing dependencies.
  - `.opencode/` tracks only `plugins/auto-commit.js`; everything else is ignored via `.opencode/.gitignore`.

## Design Docs: Single Source of Truth

- `docs/design/tech-design.md`: the main design (overview, user stories, architecture, API, component design, deployment config, observability, testing, roadmap). Implementation details follow it.
- {{Optional: `docs/design/<domain>-reference.md`: per-field reference for stable contract surfaces (API fields, config keys, protocols); terminology follows its glossary.}}
- YAML/JSON examples in the design doc are part of the contract: changing a field name requires updating the examples in the same change, and re-validating all code blocks (run them through `yaml.safe_load_all` / `json.loads`).

